            <ArticleTitle>Warden procedure for correction of sinus venosus atrial septal defect and partial anomalous pulmonary venous connection.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1510/mmcts.2016.007</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A superior sinus venosus defect is a congenital cardiac disease which is commonly associated with partial anomalous pulmonary venous connection. Here we present the Warden procedure - our preferred technique for repair. Our goal is to highlight the principles of repair with a focus on critical aspects of the surgical technique.</AbstractText>
